WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:03.651
In nuclear engineering, an assertion is not enough.

00:03.651 --> 00:11.077
Reviewers need to know which requirement supports it, which revision applies
and how the evidence connects through design

00:11.077 --> 00:13.552
substantiation, operating constraints and controlled records.

00:13.552 --> 00:16.853
That evidence remains the responsibility of authorised specialists.

00:16.853 --> 00:24.692
Cortessa is designed to help them investigate a bounded document estate,
surface documentary questions and return to the source,

00:24.692 --> 00:29.230
without becoming the design authority, the safety assessor or the regulator.

00:30.230 --> 00:36.424
A controlled plant modification or safety-case change can connect
requirements, calculations, design descriptions, operating rules,

00:36.424 --> 00:38.489
referenced standards and revision histories.

00:38.489 --> 00:43.857
Each source has an owner, status and defined role in the approval process.

00:43.857 --> 00:51.290
The practical challenge is reconstructing the chain: what wording supports the
assertion, whether the cited document is present,

00:51.290 --> 00:58.310
whether a reference has been superseded and whether apparently similar terms
mean the same thing in context.

00:59.310 --> 01:01.897
The credible evaluation is deliberately bounded.

01:01.897 --> 01:07.501
Select one change pack and use only public, synthetic or explicitly cleared
documents.

01:07.501 --> 01:13.537
Agree the authoritative corpus, revision set, expected source routes and
questions before testing begins.

01:13.537 --> 01:19.141
Define which specialists can see the material and who may adjudicate the
results.

01:19.141 --> 01:22.159
Cortessa is assessed against that fixed scope.

01:22.159 --> 01:29.919
It does not claim access to plant information, complete safety-case coverage
or suitability for classified or sensitive nuclear

01:29.919 --> 01:30.350
material.

01:31.350 --> 01:35.895
Cortessa runs on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside the agreed boundary.

01:35.895 --> 01:42.505
The approved corpus, ingestion pipeline, local index, on-device model and
source viewer remain on that machine.

01:42.505 --> 01:46.637
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:46.637 --> 01:50.768
The organisation defines the permitted documents, users and security posture.

01:50.768 --> 01:53.660
Retrieval-only operation remains available as the floor.

01:53.660 --> 02:01.510
Cortessa supports evidence review; it does not connect to plant control,
monitor operating conditions or take any operational action.

02:02.510 --> 02:05.819
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:05.819 --> 02:12.850
It works across the selected nuclear evidence chain rather than waiting for
one question at a time.

02:12.850 --> 02:18.226
It can surface stale references, supersession questions, terminology
differences and missing documentary links.

02:18.226 --> 02:24.430
Each candidate enters authorised review; it is not automatically a safety,
compliance or licence finding.

02:25.430 --> 02:29.731
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:29.731 --> 02:35.987
The authorised specialist can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and
confirm document state and context.

02:35.987 --> 02:40.678
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:40.678 --> 02:47.716
The authorised reviewer decides whether the discrepancy is genuine, material,
already resolved or outside scope, then records the

02:47.716 --> 02:49.671
outcome through the established process.

02:49.671 --> 02:53.190
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish safety significance.

02:54.190 --> 02:59.142
Safety significance, design intent and regulatory applicability require
qualified human judgement.

02:59.142 --> 03:05.444
The licensee, design authority and independent assurance functions retain
their established responsibilities and separation.

03:05.444 --> 03:10.395
Cortessa can make the evidence route and uncertainty easier to inspect.

03:10.395 --> 03:19.849
It does not approve a modification, validate a safety case, discharge a
licence condition or certify that an argument is adequate.

03:19.849 --> 03:24.350
Formal decisions and approvals remain in the organisation's controlled
systems.

03:25.350 --> 03:28.730
The operating picture should show more than an answer.

03:28.730 --> 03:35.867
Reviewers need the source route, the document state and the policy governing
what the system is allowed to present.

03:35.867 --> 03:40.374
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture are visible
governance concerns.

03:40.374 --> 03:47.135
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger to support review of what the
system did and when.

03:47.135 --> 03:50.140
That record may contribute to an evidence package.

03:50.140 --> 03:56.150
It does not make conclusions correct and does not replace nuclear records,
approvals or independent assessment.

03:57.150 --> 04:00.675
Compare matched tasks against the existing review baseline.

04:00.675 --> 04:08.605
Measure time to reconstruct an agreed assertion-to-source chain, time to
locate the current revision, reviewer effort, cited candidate

04:08.605 --> 04:12.570
findings, specialist agreement, appropriate refusals and sampled source-path
reproducibility.

04:12.570 --> 04:16.095
Include absent evidence, difficult revisions and ambiguous terminology.

04:16.095 --> 04:18.738
Record corpus preparation and setup effort.

04:18.738 --> 04:27.550
The result should identify useful support, failure modes and remediation
before any decision about a larger corpus or another workflow.

04:28.550 --> 04:30.809
Bring one cleared change pack.

04:30.809 --> 04:34.876
Agree the specialists, the baseline and the evidence standard.

04:34.876 --> 04:40.750
Test whether Cortessa helps reviewers reconstruct the source chain and
adjudicate documentary questions.

04:40.750 --> 04:46.172
Cortessa claims no nuclear deployment, regulatory approval, safety-case
acceptance or safety outcome.

04:46.172 --> 04:49.335
It never replaces the authorised decision maker.

04:49.335 --> 04:52.950
Start a conversation about a scoped nuclear evaluation.
